course: dictionary
lesson: 15567
title: Surveillance: watching with care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Surveillance means careful watching of a person, place or activity, to check for crime or danger or to collect information. Say it ser-VAY-lunss. Look at the clues in this sentence: «The shop has surveillance cameras to catch thieves.» Cameras and thieves tell you that surveillance is watching to stop crime.
explain: «The police kept the suspect under surveillance for a week.» Under surveillance means the police watched the suspect closely for a long time. The key idea is watching, so if you can picture someone keeping a close eye on something, you are near the meaning.
explain: Surveillance can also mean the equipment used for watching, such as CCTV. «The surveillance system at the station was switched on.» Here it means the cameras and machines, not the act of watching. Ask yourself: does the sentence fit better with watching or with equipment?
fact: Surveillance is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you do not add an s to make it plural.
fact: «Surveillance» means careful watching, often to check for crime or danger.
fact: CCTV is one kind of surveillance: it stands for closed-circuit television, and it is used in shops, stations and streets.
fact: «Under surveillance» means being watched closely, for example by the police.
fact: Disease surveillance means watching for outbreaks of illness, so doctors can act early.
exercise: «The shop has surveillance cameras to catch thieves.» What does surveillance mean here? | *Careful watching, often to catch crime | Sleeping in a warm bed | Buying and selling goods | Playing loud music
exercise: «The police kept the suspect under surveillance for a week.» What does under surveillance mean? | *Watched closely by someone | Given a new job at the station | Lost and forgotten | Locked in a cell for good
exercise: Mia says surveillance is just a fancy word for a camera. What is the best answer? | Surveillance is a bird that sings loudly | *Surveillance can mean the equipment, but it can also mean the watching itself | Surveillance is always a camera
test: «Scientists use disease surveillance to spot outbreaks early.» What does disease surveillance mean? | Cleaning a hospital ward | Feeling ill and tired | *Watching for outbreaks of illness | Making medicine in a lab
test: Which phrase is a good example of CCTV? | A type of bread | *A surveillance system | A kind of dance | A football team
exam: Which sentence uses surveillance to mean the cameras and equipment? | «Mum baked a cake for tea.» | «The children went to the park to play.» | *«The surveillance cameras on the platform were switched on.»
